+
+OUTPUT
+K version:    v7.1.293
+Build date:   Fri Oct 03 13:32:35 CDT 2025
+K version:    v7.1.293
+Build date:   Fri Oct 03 13:32:35 CDT 2025
+K version:    v7.1.293
+Build date:   Fri Oct 03 13:32:35 CDT 2025
+
+COMMAND
+kompile /reference/k-proof/semantic.k --backend haskell --main-module MPY-VERIFICATION --syntax-module MPY-SYNTAX --output-definition /tmp/audit-work/semantic-kompiled
+
+EXIT CODE
+0
+
+OUTPUT
+<empty>
+
+COMMAND
+krun /reference/k-proof/solution.mpy --definition /tmp/audit-work/semantic-kompiled -cINPUT='nil'
+
+EXIT CODE
+0
+
+OUTPUT
+<py>
+  <k>
+    .K
+  </k>
+  <input>
+    ListVal ( nil )
+  </input>
+  <result>
+    ListVal ( nil )
+  </result>
+</py>
+
+COMMAND
+krun /reference/k-proof/solution.mpy --definition /tmp/audit-work/semantic-kompiled -cINPUT='cons(4, nil)'
+
+EXIT CODE
+0
+
+OUTPUT
+<py>
+  <k>
+    .K
+  </k>
+  <input>
+    ListVal ( cons ( 4 , nil ) )
+  </input>
+  <result>
+    ListVal ( cons ( 4 , nil ) )
+  </result>
+</py>
+
+COMMAND
+krun /reference/k-proof/solution.mpy --definition /tmp/audit-work/semantic-kompiled -cINPUT='cons(3, cons(1, cons(2, nil)))'
+
+EXIT CODE
+0
+
+OUTPUT
+<py>
+  <k>
+    .K
+  </k>
+  <input>
+    ListVal ( cons ( 3 , cons ( 1 , cons ( 2 , nil ) ) ) )
+  </input>
+  <result>
+    ListVal ( cons ( 1 , cons ( 2 , cons ( 3 , nil ) ) ) )
+  </result>
+</py>
+
+COMMAND
+krun /reference/k-proof/solution.mpy --definition /tmp/audit-work/semantic-kompiled -cINPUT='cons(3, cons(0, cons(2, cons(1, nil))))'
+
+EXIT CODE
+0
+
+OUTPUT
+<py>
+  <k>
+    .K
+  </k>
+  <input>
+    ListVal ( cons ( 3 , cons ( 0 , cons ( 2 , cons ( 1 , nil ) ) ) ) )
+  </input>
+  <result>
+    ListVal ( cons ( 3 , cons ( 2 , cons ( 1 , cons ( 0 , nil ) ) ) ) )
+  </result>
+</py>
+
+COUNTERFACTUAL PAIR
+
+COMMAND
+krun /reference/k-proof/solution.mpy --definition /tmp/audit-work/semantic-kompiled -cINPUT='cons(1, cons(4, cons(3, nil)))'
+
+EXIT CODE
+0
+
+OUTPUT
+<py>
+  <k>
+    .K
+  </k>
+  <input>
+    ListVal ( cons ( 1 , cons ( 4 , cons ( 3 , nil ) ) ) )
+  </input>
+  <result>
+    ListVal ( cons ( 4 , cons ( 3 , cons ( 1 , nil ) ) ) )
+  </result>
+</py>
+
+COMMAND
+krun /reference/k-proof/solution.mpy --definition /tmp/audit-work/semantic-kompiled -cINPUT='cons(2, cons(4, cons(3, nil)))'
+
+EXIT CODE
+0
+
+OUTPUT
+<py>
+  <k>
+    .K
+  </k>
+  <input>
+    ListVal ( cons ( 2 , cons ( 4 , cons ( 3 , nil ) ) ) )
+  </input>
+  <result>
+    ListVal ( cons ( 2 , cons ( 3 , cons ( 4 , nil ) ) ) )
+  </result>
+</py>
+
+INTERPRETATION
+The nonempty cases preserve the input cell, compute ascending order for odd
+endpoint sum, and descending order for even endpoint sum. Changing only the
+first endpoint from 1 to 2 flips the parity and the sort direction.
